  "12_hotel_invoice.eml": {
    "_comment": [
      "Four category lines, not one 21,504 expense: policy treats each differently.",
      "",
      "Amounts come from the email body, which carries the folio as structured text. The",
      "image is the fallback for a bill that arrives as a photograph alone, and it also",
      "cross-checks this. That ordering matters here specifically: the fold drawn across",
      "hotel_invoice_1188.png destroys the second room charge under OCR, so the image alone",
      "yields 13,450 against a stated 19,200. See test_ocr_of_the_folio_loses_a_room_charge.",
      "",
      "Room charges stay aggregated with a nights count rather than being split into three",
      "invented per-night rows. The \u00a73.1 per-night limit divides by nights, so nothing is",
      "lost, and no amount is inferred from a line OCR could not read."
    ],
